<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>Geopolitical Scenario Analysis — Middle East</title>
<style>
  :root {
    --bg: #0f1117;
    --card: #1a1d27;
    --card-hover: #22263a;
    --accent: #4f8cff;
    --accent2: #ff6b6b;
    --accent3: #ffd93d;
    --accent4: #6bcb77;
    --text: #e0e0e0;
    --text-muted: #8a8fa8;
    --border: #2a2e3f;
    --red: #ff4757;
    --orange: #ffa502;
    --green: #2ed573;
    --iran: #8e44ad;
  }
  * { margin: 0; padding: 0; box-sizing: border-box; }
  body { font-family: 'Segoe UI', system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif; background: var(--bg); color: var(--text); line-height: 1.65; }
  .container { max-width: 1100px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 20px; }

  .hero { text-align: center; padding: 56px 20px 36px; background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1a1d27 0%, #0f1117 100%); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .hero h1 { font-size: 2.2em; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--accent), var(--accent2)); -webkit-background-clip: text; -webkit-text-fill-color: transparent; }
  .hero .subtitle { font-size: 1em; color: var(--text-muted); max-width: 700px; margin: 0 auto 16px; }
  .hero .date-badge { display: inline-block; background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 20px; padding: 6px 18px; font-size: 0.85em; color: var(--accent); }
  .hero .war-day { display: inline-block; background: var(--accent2); color: #fff; border-radius: 20px; padding: 6px 18px; font-size: 0.85em; font-weight: 600; margin-left: 8px; }
  .hero .build-meta { margin-top: 10px; font-size: 0.75em; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .triplet-badge { background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1a2235, #0e1a1e); border: 1px solid var(--accent); border-radius: 8px; padding: 6px 12px; font-size: 0.75em; color: var(--accent); display: inline-block; margin-top: 10px; }

  .direction-of-travel { max-width: 900px; margin: 24px auto; background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1a2235, #1a1d27); border: 2px solid var(--accent); border-radius: 12px; padding: 22px 28px; font-size: 1.05em; line-height: 1.55; }
  .direction-of-travel .label { font-size: 0.72em; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 2px; color: var(--text-muted); margin-bottom: 6px; }
  .direction-of-travel .body { color: var(--text); }
  .direction-of-travel .body .cite { color: var(--accent); font-weight: 600; font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.92em; }
  .direction-of-travel.no-move { border-color: var(--border); }
  .direction-of-travel.no-move .body { color: var(--text-muted); font-style: italic; }

  .disclaimer { background: #2a1a1a; border: 1px solid #5a2020; border-radius: 12px; padding: 16px 20px; margin: 24px auto; max-width: 900px; font-size: 0.85em; color: #ffaaaa; }
  .disclaimer strong { color: var(--accent2); }

  .section { padding: 30px 0; }
  .section-title { font-size: 1.5em; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 18px; padding-bottom: 8px; border-bottom: 2px solid var(--accent); display: flex; align-items: baseline; justify-content: space-between; }
  .section-title .meta { font-size: 0.6em; color: var(--text-muted); font-weight: 400; }

  /* === FORECAST BOARD === */
  .forecast-board { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px; }
  .forecast-bucket-label { font-size: 0.75em; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1.5px; color: var(--text-muted); margin: 14px 0 4px; padding-left: 4px; }
  .forecast-bucket-label:first-child { margin-top: 0; }
  .forecast-card { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-left: 4px solid var(--accent); border-radius: 10px; padding: 16px 20px; }
  .forecast-card.cat-diplomacy { border-left-color: var(--accent); }
  .forecast-card.cat-military { border-left-color: var(--red); }
  .forecast-card.cat-regime { border-left-color: var(--iran); }
  .forecast-card.cat-market { border-left-color: var(--accent3); }
  .forecast-card.cat-domestic { border-left-color: var(--accent4); }
  .forecast-card.cat-humanitarian { border-left-color: var(--orange); }
  .forecast-card .fc-head { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: baseline; gap: 12px; margin-bottom: 6px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .forecast-card .fc-id { font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.7em; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card .fc-category { font-size: 0.7em; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1px; color: var(--text-muted); padding: 2px 8px; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 4px; }
  .forecast-card .fc-question { font-size: 1em; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text); margin: 6px 0 10px; line-height: 1.45; }
  .forecast-card .fc-probrow { display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 18px; margin-bottom: 8px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .forecast-card .fc-p { font-size: 1.8em; font-weight: 800; color: var(--accent); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta { font-size: 0.9em; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta.move-up { color: var(--red); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta.move-down { color: var(--green); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta.no-move { color: var(--border); }
  .forecast-card .fc-horizon { font-size: 0.85em; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta-reason { font-size: 0.92em; color: var(--text); margin: 6px 0 10px; }
  .forecast-card .fc-meta-row { font-size: 0.8em; color: var(--text-muted); display: grid; grid-template-columns: max-content 1fr; gap: 4px 12px; margin-top: 8px; padding-top: 10px; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .forecast-card .fc-meta-row dt { font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card .fc-meta-row dd { color: var(--text); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicators { font-size: 0.82em; color: var(--text-muted); margin-top: 6px; }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator { display: inline-block; padding: 2px 8px; margin: 2px; border-radius: 4px; border: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator.state-OBSERVED { background: rgba(46, 213, 115, 0.15); border-color: var(--green); color: var(--green); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator.state-PARTIAL { background: rgba(255, 165, 2, 0.15); border-color: var(--orange); color: var(--orange); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator.state-CONTRADICTED { background: rgba(255, 71, 87, 0.15); border-color: var(--red); color: var(--red); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator.state-NOT_OBSERVED { color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card.status-OBE { opacity: 0.55; border-left-style: dashed; }
  .forecast-card.status-OBE .fc-question::after { content: ' [OBE]'; color: var(--text-muted); font-style: italic; }
  .forecast-empty-slot { background: transparent; border: 1px dashed var(--border); border-radius: 10px; padding: 14px 20px; color: var(--text-muted); font-style: italic; font-size: 0.88em; }

  /* === DELTA SECTION === */
  .delta-narrative p { color: var(--text); font-size: 0.96em; margin-bottom: 14px; }
  .delta-narrative p .cite { color: var(--accent); font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.88em; }
  .delta-narrative p .context-only { color: var(--text-muted); font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.85em; }

  /* === SCENARIO MAP === */
  .scenario-map { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; padding: 18px 22px; }
  .prob-bar-container { display: flex; height: 36px; border-radius: 8px; overflow: hidden; margin: 8px 0 14px; }
  .prob-bar { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; font-weight: 700; font-size: 0.85em; color: #fff; }
  .prob-escalation { background: var(--red); }
  .prob-status { background: var(--orange); }
  .prob-deescalation { background: var(--green); }
  .scenario-line { font-size: 0.92em; color: var(--text); margin-bottom: 6px; }
  .scenario-line strong.label-esc { color: var(--red); }
  .scenario-line strong.label-prot { color: var(--orange); }
  .scenario-line strong.label-desc { color: var(--green); }

  /* === INSIDE IRAN === */
  .inside-iran { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-left: 4px solid var(--iran); border-radius: 10px; padding: 18px 22px; }
  .inside-iran p { font-size: 0.93em; margin-bottom: 12px; }
  .inside-iran p .cite { color: var(--accent); font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.85em; }
  .iran-media-badges { display: flex; gap: 6px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-bottom: 12px; }
  .iran-media-badge { display: inline-block; padding: 2px 8px; border: 1px solid var(--iran); border-radius: 4px; font-size: 0.72em; color: var(--iran); }

  /* === REGIME CHANGE WATCH === */
  .regime-watch { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; padding: 18px 22px; }
  .regime-watch-meta { font-size: 0.8em; color: var(--text-muted); margin-bottom: 14px; }
  .regime-row { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: baseline; padding: 10px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px; }
  .regime-row:last-child { border-bottom: 0; }
  .regime-row .name { font-weight: 600; }
  .regime-row .p { font-size: 1.4em; font-weight: 700; color: var(--orange); }
  .regime-row .drivers { font-size: 0.85em; color: var(--text-muted); flex-basis: 100%; margin-top: 4px; }

  /* === SOURCES === */
  .sources-list { list-style: none; padding: 0; }
  .sources-list li { padding: 8px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); font-size: 0.88em; display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 10px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .sources-list a { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: none; }
  .sources-list a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
  .source-tier { display: inline-block; padding: 1px 8px; border-radius: 4px; font-size: 0.7em; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.5px; flex-shrink: 0; }
  .source-tier.tier-TIER1 { background: rgba(46, 213, 115, 0.15); color: var(--green); border: 1px solid var(--green); }
  .source-tier.tier-OSINT { background: rgba(79, 140, 255, 0.15); color: var(--accent); border: 1px solid var(--accent); }
  .source-tier.tier-STATE_MEDIA { background: rgba(255, 165, 2, 0.15); color: var(--orange); border: 1px solid var(--orange); }
  .source-tier.tier-EXPERT { background: rgba(155, 89, 182, 0.15); color: #9b59b6; border: 1px solid #9b59b6; }

  /* === EXPERT APPENDIX === */
  .expert-appendix { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; margin-top: 18px; }
  .expert-appendix summary { padding: 14px 20px; cursor: pointer; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.92em; user-select: none; }
  .expert-appendix summary:hover { color: var(--text); }
  .expert-appendix[open] summary { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .expert-appendix .expert-body { padding: 14px 20px 18px; }
  .expert-quote { padding: 10px 14px; border-left: 3px solid #9b59b6; margin-bottom: 12px; font-size: 0.9em; }
  .expert-quote .expert-name { font-weight: 700; color: #9b59b6; margin-bottom: 4px; }
  .expert-empty { color: var(--text-muted); font-style: italic; font-size: 0.88em; }

  /* === FOOTER === */
  footer { text-align: center; padding: 32px 20px; color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.8em; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); margin-top: 32px; }
  footer .next-update { color: var(--accent); }

  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .hero { padding: 36px 16px 24px; }
    .hero h1 { font-size: 1.5em; line-height: 1.3; }
    .container { padding: 12px; }
    .direction-of-travel { margin: 16px 12px; padding: 16px 18px; font-size: 0.95em; }
    .disclaimer { margin: 16px 12px; padding: 12px; font-size: 0.8em; }
    .section-title { font-size: 1.2em; }
    .forecast-card { padding: 14px 16px; }
    .forecast-card .fc-p { font-size: 1.5em; }
    .scenario-map, .inside-iran, .regime-watch, .expert-appendix .expert-body { padding: 14px 16px; }
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="hero">
  <h1>Geopolitical Scenario Analysis — Middle East</h1>
  <p class="subtitle">Forecast board + descriptive delta. Predictions are time-bounded and scored; descriptions are sourced and verb-disciplined.</p>
  <span class="date-badge">October 5, 2026</span>
  <span class="war-day">Day 220 of Operation Epic Fury</span>
  <div class="build-meta">Published: <span id="pub-ts">2026-10-05T07:05Z</span> · Build <span id="build-id" style="font-family:monospace;opacity:0.6;">v49.0</span></div>
  <div class="triplet-badge">&#9878; Triple-blind: Analyst + Devil&rsquo;s Advocate + Judge &middot; forecast-board v45</div>
</div>

<div class="container">

  <!-- ========== 1. DIRECTION OF TRAVEL ========== -->
  <div class="direction-of-travel">
    <div class="label">Where this is heading</div>
    <div class="body">
      Military lull holds ahead of the November midterms — <span class="cite">F9</span> (US large-scale strikes by Nov 10, p=28%) outpaces <span class="cite">F8</span> (Iran-US deal by Oct 27, p=9%) — while Israel&rsquo;s October 27 vote narrows with <span class="cite">F5</span> (Likud plurality, p=35%) and <span class="cite">F10</span> (opposition bloc majority, p=35%) both reflecting a near-coin-flip outcome.
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="disclaimer">
    <strong>&#9888; DISCLAIMER:</strong> This analysis relies on open sources (OSINT) and AI-generated assessments. Probabilities are time-bounded forecasts with resolution criteria; track record visible internally until &ge;20 forecasts resolve. Descriptive sections enforce verb discipline &mdash; any causal/directional claim must cite a forecast or be marked context-only.
  </div>

  <!-- ========== 2. FORECAST BOARD ========== -->
  <div class="section" id="forecast-board">
    <h2 class="section-title">
      Forecast Board
      <span class="meta">5 active &middot; 3 resolved today &middot; 1 retired (OBE) &middot; 4 new &middot; last reasoned 2026-10-05</span>
    </h2>

    <div class="forecast-board">

      <!-- NEAR-TERM (≤72h) -->
      <div class="forecast-bucket-label">NEAR-TERM (&le;72h)</div>
      <div class="forecast-empty-slot">No publishable forecast in this horizon today.</div>

      <!-- 7-30 DAYS -->
      <div class="forecast-bucket-label">7&ndash;30 DAYS</div>

      <!-- F8: Iran-US preliminary agreement by Oct 27 (22 days) -->
      <div class="forecast-card cat-diplomacy status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">F8 &middot; 2026-10-05-iran-us-preliminary-agreement-before-oct27</span>
          <span class="fc-category">diplomacy</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will Iran and the US reach a preliminary written agreement (ceasefire deal-framework, MoU, or joint communiqu&eacute; confirmed by both parties) before EOD 2026-10-27?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">9%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta no-move">NEW &middot; p=0.09 (2026-10-05)</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">→ resolves by 2026-10-27</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">New forecast. Trump publicly rejected Iran&rsquo;s 7-day Hormuz proposal on Oct 1 and explicitly threatened resumed strikes post-November midterms. Iran received a US counterproposal and is reviewing it; Deputy FM Gharibabadi confirmed receipt Oct 4, stating &ldquo;the ball is in the United States&rsquo; court.&rdquo; Trump stated Oct 3&ndash;4 he would review Iran&rsquo;s 14-point plan but &ldquo;can&rsquo;t imagine it would be acceptable.&rdquo; The primary sticking point is nuclear sequencing: US insists nuclear program addressed first; Iran insists on sequencing that defers nuclear talks. A formal agreement before Oct 27 is possible but probability is very low given Trump&rsquo;s explicit public posture and the Iranian delegation expulsion.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>A public written agreement &mdash; ceasefire MoU, framework deal, or joint statement establishing conditions for ending hostilities &mdash; signed or jointly announced by Iran and the US (or designated mediators with both parties confirming). Unilateral announcements disputed by the other party do not qualify. Verbal commitments alone do not qualify.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>Resolve YES on &ge;2 TIER1 sources (Reuters, AP, AFP, Bloomberg) AND official statements from both US State Department/White House and Iranian Foreign Ministry/IRNA.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>If one party announces a deal but the other disputes its terms or existence, resolve AMBIGUOUS. If a deal is announced after Oct 27 but backdated, resolve NO. If negotiations are confirmed active but no deal is concluded by EOD Oct 27, resolve NO.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Iran formally responds to US counterproposal</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Confirmed indirect Iran-US session via Qatar or Pakistan</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Trump withdraws post-midterm strike threat</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- F10: Opposition bloc ≥61 seats (23 days) -->
      <div class="forecast-card cat-domestic status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">F10 &middot; 2026-10-05-opposition-bloc-knesset-majority-oct27</span>
          <span class="fc-category">domestic</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will the Israeli opposition bloc led by Eisenkot&rsquo;s Yashar win &ge;61 seats in the October 27, 2026 Knesset election?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">35%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta no-move">NEW &middot; p=0.35 (2026-10-05)</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">→ resolves by 2026-10-28</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">New forecast capturing bloc-level outcome distinct from F5 (party-level plurality). Current polling projects the opposition bloc at 58&ndash;64 seats &mdash; straddling the 61-seat majority threshold. The key variable is Arab List behavior: formal cooperation brings the bloc to 61+; Arab abstention or neutrality leaves it short. Netanyahu&rsquo;s explicit strategy is deadlock (neither bloc reaches 61), which he treats as a governing win. Opposition bloc majority win is plausible but not probable at current polling.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>Parties publicly committed to supporting Eisenkot as PM (core: Yashar, Together, Democrats, Yisrael Beytenu, plus publicly committed Arab party external support) win &ge;61 combined seats per Israeli Central Elections Committee certified results.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>Central Elections Committee certified results; Haaretz, Jerusalem Post, Times of Israel as preliminary indicators within 72h of publication.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>If bloc wins exactly 61 but one member defects before formation, still resolve YES (election, not formation). Arab external support counts if publicly committed before election day. Disputed results: delay until certified.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-PARTIAL">Poll-of-polls showing opposition bloc consistently &ge;61 seats</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Arab List formal commitment to Eisenkot government</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Netanyahu trial adverse ruling before Oct 27</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- 30-90 DAYS -->
      <div class="forecast-bucket-label">30&ndash;90 DAYS</div>

      <!-- F9: US large-scale strikes by Nov 10 (36 days) -->
      <div class="forecast-card cat-military status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">F9 &middot; 2026-10-05-us-large-scale-strikes-iran-before-nov10</span>
          <span class="fc-category">military</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will US forces execute a large-scale (&ge;24-hour sustained) offensive air campaign against targets inside Iran before EOD 2026-11-10?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">28%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta no-move">NEW &middot; p=0.28 (2026-10-05)</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">→ resolves by 2026-11-10</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">New forecast. Trump explicitly stated Oct 1&ndash;3 that strikes on Iran could resume after the November 4 midterm elections if a deal is not reached. The USS Theodore Roosevelt CSG and Makin Island ARG were dispatched Oct 1 with ~9,000&ndash;10,000 additional personnel, joining the George H.W. Bush and George Washington already on station. Senior Trump administration officials met at Camp David Oct 3&ndash;4 to discuss Iran war strategy. GlobalSecurity Day 218 confirms 26 consecutive days without a coalition strike on Iranian territory ashore. The lull most plausibly reflects a political pause tied to midterm election calculus. Probability at 0.28: meaningful but below 0.50, reflecting genuine possibility that Trump&rsquo;s threat is leverage rather than intention.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>US forces conduct a sustained offensive air campaign lasting &ge;24 consecutive hours with multiple sorties targeting hardened military infrastructure, nuclear facilities, or IRGC installations on Iranian territory. A single drone strike on border positions or at-sea interdiction does not qualify. Requires CENTCOM press release confirming strikes on Iranian territory.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>CENTCOM official press release confirming strikes on Iranian territory + &ge;1 TIER1 corroborating; CENTCOM PR alone suffices if confirmed by DoD official statement.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>Strikes on Iranian-aligned proxies only (not Iranian territory) = NO. Strikes after Nov 10 = NO for this forecast. Coordinated with Israel but US role confirmed primary by CENTCOM = YES; US role secondary only = NO.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Trump post-midterm order to resume Iran campaign</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">USS Theodore Roosevelt arrives in CENTCOM AOR early</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Iran rejects US counterproposal with hostile statement</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Deal framework agreed before Nov 4 (reduces to 0.05)</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- F5: Likud plurality (54 days from creation, 22 days remaining) -->
      <div class="forecast-card cat-domestic status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">F5 &middot; 2026-09-03-likud-plurality-oct27-election</span>
          <span class="fc-category">domestic</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will Likud win the most Knesset seats (seat plurality) in the October 27, 2026 Israeli election?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">35%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta move-down">&darr; 7pp from 42% (2026-09-03)</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">→ resolves by 2026-10-27</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">UPDATE (p 0.42→0.35). Polling through Oct 4 shows a volatile near-tie. Four of five recent polls average Yashar (Eisenkot) at 23&ndash;24 seats vs Likud at 21&ndash;23, with Yashar holding the multi-poll-average lead. Two individual polls (KAN News, Channel 12, both Oct 4) reversed the average lead, placing Likud at 24 seats and Yashar at 22&ndash;23. At the bloc level, most surveys project the opposition at ~62 seats vs Netanyahu bloc ~48&ndash;55. The October 7 third anniversary cycle (ceremonies, inquiry narrative) has activated anti-Netanyahu constituencies. Probability reduced from 0.42 to 0.35: a near-coin-flip race in individual polls but a clear Yashar edge in the multi-poll average.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if Israeli Central Elections Committee official results show Likud winning more seats than any other single party in the October 27, 2026 election.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>Central Elections Committee official results, carried by Times of Israel/Haaretz/Reuters/AP.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>If Likud and one other party tie on seats: AMBIGUOUS-RESOLVE-AS-NO. Exit polls alone do not resolve; official preliminary results suffice if published before EOD Oct 27.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-PARTIAL">Poll average: Likud &ge;23 seats, ahead of Yashar (contested)</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Likud bloc coalition-eligible alliance pre-election</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-PARTIAL">Yashar averaging 23&ndash;24 seats (leading in poll avg)</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- F11: Hormuz ≥15 transits by Nov 30 (56 days) -->
      <div class="forecast-card cat-market status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">F11 &middot; 2026-10-05-hormuz-15-transits-before-nov30</span>
